# Scenario for scripts/record-scenario.py: the F8 has no address bus.
# PC0, PC1 (P) and DC live in the memory devices; the CPU only sends
# them ROMC commands, so every address in a dump is one the debugger
# rebuilt from those commands. Its hardware call stack is one level --
# PI parks the return address in PC1 -- so these samples nest calls
# through a software trampoline, "pi call" + "da target".
#
# ADDRESSES ARE PINNED TO THE CURRENT samples/f3850/mandelbrot.hex:
# call (stack.inc) at 0323, the "pi call / da mulsi2" in loop_x at
# 06D4. If mandelbrot.asm/.inc/stack.inc/.hex ever change, re-check
# them against the fresh .lst before recording -- a stale address will
# look like it works (it disassembles *something*) while showing the
# wrong thing.

key ?
pace 2.0

key R
upload samples/f3850/mandelbrot.hex

# The trampoline: LR K,P takes PC1 -- the address of the "da" operand
# that PI left there -- and LR DC,H points DC at it, so the two LMs read
# the call target out of the instruction stream and LR P,K makes it the
# return point of the POP that ends the routine.
type D
wait Disassemble?
command 0323 12
pace 2.0

# Stop on the call, then step: PI sets P0 to the trampoline and P to the
# operand; the LMs walk DC across the embedded address; after LR P,K,
# P holds mulsi2 (04DE), ready for POP to jump there.
type g
wait Go until?
command 06D4 5
pace 0.9
step 12
pace 1.5

# Watch one frame render -- a full frame measured at ~817s on real
# hardware, hence the long wait.
run 1 1200
